  characterName: Thakur Mohamed
  promptText: Tourists are breaking coral for souvenirs; reef degradation accelerates
    while local guides rely on visitors for income. Enforcing a ban would protect
    ecosystem function but remove the immediate livelihoods tourists provide.
  leftAnswer: Safeguarding the reef sustains food and life beyond short-term profit.
  rightAnswer: Keeping tourism preserves incomes that families depend on today.
